module

public import WeilConjectures.AlgebraicGeometry.FunctionField
public import Sheaf.TraceFormula.LocalDimensionFormula
public import Mathlib.FieldTheory.AlgebraicClosure
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.IntegralClosure.IntegrallyClosed
import WeilConjectures.Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.FunctionField
import Mathlib.RingTheory.Algebraic.Integral
import Mathlib.RingTheory.IntegralClosure.Algebra.Basic

/-! # Algebraic constants from finite global sections of a normal integral scheme

Source: Stacks Project, properties.tex, Tag 0358, lemma-normal-integral-sections,
adapted to algebraicity over the base fraction field; fields.tex, Tags 09GG, 09GI,
and 09GJ (blueprint: lem-sfb-normal-sections-algebraic-constants).

The base fraction field is the generic stalk of `Spec A`. The fraction field of the
ring of global sections, inside the function field, is the subfield generated by its
generic germs. Both inclusions are the canonical pullback maps.
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u

open CategoryTheory

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-- For a dominant morphism from an integral scheme with integrally closed local
rings to the spectrum of a domain, finite global sections have fraction field equal
to the relative algebraic closure of the base fraction field in the function field.
This extension is finite and algebraically closed inside the function field, and an
algebraic element becomes a global section after multiplication by a nonzero base element.
Source: Stacks Project, properties.tex, Tag 0358, lemma-normal-integral-sections,
relative adaptation; fields.tex, Tags 09GG, 09GI, 09GJ
(blueprint: lem-sfb-normal-sections-algebraic-constants).

Proof: the generic germ embeds the global sections into the function field, by
`lem-sc-integral-scheme-stalks-in-function-field`. The finite-domain fraction-degree
lemma `lem-trf-finite-domain-fraction-degree` makes their fraction field finite over
the base fraction field. Thus every element of it is algebraic, using
`lem-weil-pbc-finite-algebra-is-integral` over that base field.
Conversely, normalize a nonzero annihilating polynomial for an algebraic element
`a` to be monic. Write its coefficients as fractions over `A` and take their common
nonzero denominator `d`. If its degree is `n` and coefficients are `c_i`, then `d*a`
satisfies a monic equation with coefficients `d^(n-i)*c_i` in `A`. Map the equation
into each local ring. Its fraction field is the function field by
`lem-sc-integral-scheme-stalks-in-function-field`, and integral closedness puts `d*a`
in every local ring. Apply `lem-sc-function-field-sections-glue` on the whole scheme
to obtain a global section `r` with generic germ `d*a`. Hence `a=r/d` belongs to the
fraction field of the global sections. This proves the equality with the relative
algebraic closure and the specified denominator assertion. Finally, if an element
is algebraic over this finite field extension, `lem-sfb-algebraic-element-tower`
makes it algebraic over the base fraction field, so the equality puts it in the
same intermediate field. -/
theorem normal_sections_algebraic_constants
    (A : Type u) [CommRing A] [IsDomain A]
    (X : Scheme.{u}) [IsIntegral X]
    (h : X ⟶ Spec (CommRingCat.of A)) [IsDominant h]
    (hX : ∀ x : X, IsIntegrallyClosed (X.presheaf.stalk x))
    (hfin : @Module.Finite A Γ(X, ⊤) _ _
      (((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of A)).inv ≫ h.appTop).hom.toAlgebra.toModule)) :
    ∃ e : Algebra (Spec (CommRingCat.of A)).functionField X.functionField,
      e = h.dominantFunctionFieldAlgebra ∧
      ∃ L : IntermediateField (Spec (CommRingCat.of A)).functionField X.functionField,
      L.toSubfield =
        Subfield.closure (Set.range (X.presheaf.germ ⊤ (genericPoint X) (by trivial))) ∧
      L = algebraicClosure (Spec (CommRingCat.of A)).functionField X.functionField ∧
      FiniteDimensional (Spec (CommRingCat.of A)).functionField L ∧
      (∀ a : X.functionField, IsAlgebraic L a → a ∈ L) ∧
      ∀ a : X.functionField,
        IsAlgebraic (Spec (CommRingCat.of A)).functionField a →
        ∃ d : A, d ≠ 0 ∧ ∃ r : Γ(X, ⊤),
          X.presheaf.germ ⊤ (genericPoint X) (by trivial) r =
            X.presheaf.germ ⊤ (genericPoint X) (by trivial)
              (((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of A)).inv ≫ h.appTop) d) * a := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry
